VectorCraft VAIO preview 0.13.1

Open VectorCraft (VAIO preview) from Graphics or VAIO App Launcher. Ctrl+O opens,
Ctrl+S saves, and Save As chooses another filename. Use .vectorcraft for the native
editable model; older .drawcraft files remain readable. SVG, PDF and raster export
provide exchange formats. Keep original files when exchanging complex artwork.

This unofficial build selects OpenGL/Glow for the interface and retains the upstream
CPU drawing engine, commands and format modules. Its initial window fits the VAIO.
vectorcraft-vaio-cli provides headless batch conversion and explicit headless MCP;
the desktop entry does not start an automation server.

Bundled upstream open fonts and eight pinned craft-fonts fallback faces retain their
original licence and attribution notices. No proprietary application assets are used.

This is upstream alpha software. Very complex illustrations, external proprietary
format fidelity, physical printing, colour-critical output and third-party plugins
remain unverified. The VAIO uses software rendering; larger artwork may be slow.

Updates use the signed APT source and the existing Check & Install Updates tool.
Remove with sudo apt-get remove vectorcraft-vaio; user files/settings are retained.
